WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.322
The inner query calculates average age across all patients.

00:00:03.322 --> 00:00:09.197
That produces one number. The outer WHERE clause compares each patient age with that one benchmark.

00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:15.727
Read the condition as a sentence: keep the patient when age is greater than the average age returned by the

00:00:15.727 --> 00:00:21.637
inner query. Run the query and compare the returned ages with the full patient list.

00:00:21.637 --> 00:00:23.022
A subquery has a contract: it returns a shape.

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:27.172
A scalar subquery must return at most one value where it is used.

00:00:27.172 --> 00:00:33.337
Before writing syntax, predict whether the inner query returns one value, one column with many rows,

00:00:33.337 --> 00:00:38.956
or a table. Shape mistakes are easier to prevent than to debug after the query becomes large.
